      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed.— source of truth. Req ID prefix: **PAY**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n| Req ID | Sub-Functional Area | Requirement | Owner | Storefront | Config/Custom | Status | **Comments** | **User Stories** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PAY-001 | Payment Methods | The system will present available payment methods at the payment step of checkout, configured per storefront in SFCC Business Manager. | Zimmerman | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-001> |\n| PAY-002 | Payment Methods | The system will support Credit/Debit Card payment (Visa, Mastercard, American Express) via Adyen on all domestic storefronts. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-002> |\n| PAY-003 | Payment Methods | The system will support PayPal payment via Adyen on all domestic storefronts. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-003> |\n| PAY-004 | Payment Methods | The system will support Apple Pay Express via Adyen in the mini bag on eligible devices | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-004> |\n| PAY-005 | Payment Methods | The system will support Apple Pay via Adyen at checkout on all storefronts and eligible web browsers (note: currently targeting August 2026) | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-005> |\n| PAY-006 | Payment Methods | The system will support Google Pay and Google Pay Express via Adyen across all storefronts and eligible devices (note: currently targeting August 2026) | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-006> |\n| PAY-007 | Payment Methods | The system will support BNPL via Klarna on AU and US storefronts (note: currently targeting August 2026) | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-007> |\n| PAY-008 | Payment Methods | The system will handle payment failure states gracefully, displaying clear error messaging and allowing the client to retry or select an alternative payment method without losing order data. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-008> |\n| PAY-009 | Payment Methods | The system will not invoke Adyen or PayPal for Global-e-managed international orders — Global-e handles all payment processing for international orders. | Tryzens | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-009> |\n| PAY-010 | Payment Methods | This system will support the following payment options at checkout: Full payment: This system will allow customers to pay in full via credit card, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay, digital or physical gift card, credit note, or Retail Rewards (full balance redemption). | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-010> |\n| PAY-011 | Payment Methods | This system will support the following payment options at checkout: Split payment: This system will allow customers to combine any gift card, credit note, or Retail Rewards (full balance redemption) with any external payment method (credit card, PayPal, Apple Pay or Google Pay). | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-011> |\n| PAY-011a | Payment Methods | This system will prevent customers from purchasing a digital or physical gift card using a gift card as a payment method. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-011a> |\n| PAY-011b | Payment Methods | This system will remove the gift card payment option at checkout when a gift card is present in the customer's cart. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-011b> |\n| PAY-012 | Payment Methods | The system will pass Level 2 (tax amount) and Level 3 (itemised order lines) data to Adyen in the payment payload to support interchange fee optimisation. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-012> |\n| PAY-013 | Payment Methods | The system will pass all required order details to Adyen to enable Adyen's fraud rule engine (RevenueProtect) to apply all configured risk controls. Fraud rules, thresholds, velocity checks, transaction limits, and risk scoring are owned and managed entirely within Adyen - SFCC passes data and responds to Adyen's outcome only. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-013> |\n| PAY-014 | Payment Methods | The system will place no limit on the number of payment retries a customer can attempt within a checkout session - retry behaviour is managed natively by Adyen Drop-In. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-014> |\n| PAY-015 | Payment Methods | The system will detect when a shipping address entered during checkout does not match the expected region for the storefront, and surface a clear error or warning to the customer before order completion. For express payment methods (Apple Pay Express, Google Pay Express), where address validation occurs post-payment authorisation, the system will reject the transaction at the Adyen level if the address does not match the eligible storefront region. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-015> |\n| ~~PAY-016~~ | ~~Payment Methods~~ | ~~The system will support Pay by Link via Adyen for manual orders, allowing the Ops or CS team to send a payment link directly to the customer to complete payment outside of the standard storefront checkout flow.~~ | ~~Zimmerman~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | descoped, OOBO is out of scope | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-016> |\n| PAY-017 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will display saved payment methods at the payment step for registered clients who have previously saved a card, allowing selection of a saved card without re-entering card details. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-017> |\n| PAY-018 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will allow clients to save a new card during checkout by selecting a \"Save this card to your account for faster checkout\" option. This option will be unchecked by default. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-018> |\n| PAY-019 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will allow clients to manage (view and remove) saved payment methods via My Account, displaying card type, last four digits, and expiry date sourced from Adyen via token reference. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-019> |\n| PAY-020 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will allow clients to remove saved payment methods from My Account, with the corresponding token deleted in Adyen. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-020> |\n| PAY-021 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will not store raw card data in SFCC; saved card tokens are held in Adyen and surfaced to SFCC via token reference only. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-021> |\n| PAY-022 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | ~~The system will not re-challenge the customer with 3DS authentication when paying with a previously saved card, where Adyen has remembered the prior authentication.~~ The system will require the customer to re-enter the CVV for any previously saved card at the point of payment. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-022> |\n| PAY-023 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will support PayPal at the payment step via Adyen; the customer will be redirected to PayPal for authentication and returned to the SFCC checkout with payment confirmed. Billing address data from the PayPal callback will be pre-populated where available. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-023> |\n| PAY-024 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will allow the packaging default option (Eco or Signature) for a particular payment method to be configurable per storefront in SFCC Business Manager. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-024> |\n| PAY-025 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will allow packaging options (Eco and Signature) to be switched on or off per storefront in SFCC Business Manager | Zimmerman | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-025> |\n| PAY-026 | Saved Cards & Digital Wallets | The system will allow the frontend display copy for packaging options (e.g. option labels and descriptions) to be edited per storefront in SFCC Business Manager | Zimmerman | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-026> |\n| PAY-027 | Retail Rewards | The system will automatically apply the customer's full Retail Rewards balance at the payment step for eligible Gold and Platinum VIP members. The customer will have the option to remove the applied balance before completing the order. Where the Retail Rewards balance exceeds the cart value, only the amount required to cover the order will be redeemed. Retail Rewards can be combined with credit cards, gift cards, credit notes and promo codes. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-027> |\n| PAY-028 | Retail Rewards | The system will display the Gold VIP loyalty discount as a separate named line item in the order summary during checkout (e.g. \"DISCOUNT | GOLD VIP - 10% OFF\"), showing the discount amount deducted from the subtotal. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-028> |\n| PAY-029 | Retail Rewards | The system will require an additional payment method (credit card, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay, or gift card/credit note) to cover the remaining balance where the Retail Rewards balance is less than the order total. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-029> |\n| PAY-030 | Retail Rewards | The system will not require an additional payment method where the Retail Rewards balance covers the full order total. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-030> |\n| PAY-031 | Retail Rewards | The system will validate the Retail Rewards balance in real-time via AP21 at the point of automatic application at the payment step. The validation will occur at point of transaction to prevent a customer from applying the same balance across multiple concurrent orders. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-031> |\n| PAY-032 | Retail Rewards | The system will apply the Retail Rewards voucher payment method before tax calculation for US orders, as US sales tax is variable by state. For all other domestic storefronts, the discount is applied post-tax. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-032> |\n| PAY-033 | Retail Rewards | The system will handle AP21 unavailability gracefully at the Retail Rewards validation step - if the balance cannot be retrieved, the customer will be informed and able to proceed with an alternative payment method without losing their order. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-033> |\n| PAY-034 | Retail Rewards | The system will display the customer's Loyalty Status tier name and a brief description of tier benefits on the My Account dashboard. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-034> |\n| PAY-035 | Retail Rewards | The system will display the customer's total available Retail Rewards balance on the My Account dashboard with the message that the balance is updated on every login. The balance will reflect the sum of all unredeemed individual vouchers. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-035> |\n| PAY-036 | Retail Rewards | The system will refund the customer via the original payment method used at the time of purchase. Where Retail Rewards were applied, the redeemed balance will be returned to the customer's Retail Rewards account for the same value used. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-036> |\n| PAY-037 | Retail Rewards | The system will display Retail Rewards balance and transaction history in the customer's My Orders section in My Account, for eligible Gold and Platinum VIP members. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-037> |\n| PAY-038 | Retail Rewards | The system will display a breakdown table of individual vouchers in My Account showing: Voucher Description, Amount Issued, Amount Used, Amount Remaining, and Expiry Date. Vouchers will be ordered by soonest expiry. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-038> |\n| PAY-039 | Retail Rewards | The system will display messaging in My Account for customers on Global-e-operated storefronts (HK, ME, EU International) directing VIP clients to contact Client Services to redeem Retail Rewards, as online redemption is not supported on these storefronts. | Accenture | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-039> |\n| PAY-040 | Retail Rewards | The system will treat Retail Rewards as a separate payment mechanism from GiveX gift cards - a single checkout may invoke both a GiveX call (gift card) and a Retail Rewards call (AP21) independently. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-040> |\n| PAY-041 | Fraud Management | The system will pass payment data through Adyen RevenueProtect on every domestic order for fraud screening. All fraud rule configuration, thresholds, velocity checks, and risk decisioning are owned entirely within Adyen — SFCC has no role in fraud rule management. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-041> |\n| PAY-042 | Fraud Management | The system will pass the customer group attribute to Adyen in the payment request payload to enable group-specific fraud risk scoring. Custom fraud rules are confirmed to exist in Adyen, implemented as shared rules targeted by country/market. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-042> |\n| PAY-042a | Fraud Management | The system will pass all required shopper and order data attributes to Adyen in the payment request to support fraud rule evaluation, including shopper name, email address, phone number, billing address, delivery address, and registered country. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-042a> |\n| PAY-043 | Fraud Management | The system will pass an isGiftCard=TRUE flag to Adyen when a gift card payment instrument is included in the transaction. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-043> |\n| PAY-044 | Fraud Management | The system will place all orders containing a gift card product purchase (physical or digital) into fraud review - fulfilment and gift card code delivery will be withheld until the review is resolved. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed | should be de-scoped, Adyen functionality | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-044> |\n| PAY-045 | Fraud Management | The system will support 3DS authentication inline via Adyen Drop-In where triggered by the card issuer or Adyen risk rules, without redirecting the client away from checkout. | Dependent SF Functionality | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-044> |\n| PAY-046 | Fraud Management | The system will not handle Adyen fraud webhook notifications directly - fraud event processing is routed via MuleSoft. SFCC has no role in fraud hold monitoring or timing. | Mule Integrator | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-046> |\n| PAY-047 | Fraud Management | The system will create the order and send it to NewStore immediately upon payment authorisation. NewStore will hold the order and reserve inventory for the duration of the fraud review period. No auto-cancellation occurs. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom |  | @Jasmijn Tsang Should be de-scoped, this is Adyen. Might be worth confirming SFCC role here v Adyen | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-047> |\n| PAY-048 | Fraud Management | The system will support a fraud hold period with no fixed maximum duration - hold duration is determined by the Ops team review timeline and may extend beyond 48 hours in practice. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom |  | @Jasmijn Tsang should be de-scoped, this is Adyen functionality | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-048> |\n| PAY-049 | Fraud Management | The system will not send any customer-facing communication during an active fraud hold - the customer will receive no notification that their order is under review. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom |  | @Jasmijn Tsang should be de-scoped, not SFCC. | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-049> |\n| PAY-050 | Fraud Management | The system will, upon Ops team approval of a fraud-flagged order in the Adyen dashboard, route the approval via MuleSoft to NewStore OMS to release the order for fulfilment. SFCC will receive the updated order status from NewStore OMS and reflect this to the customer. | Mule Integrator | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-050> |\n| PAY-051 | Fraud Management | The system will, upon Ops team rejection of a fraud-flagged order in the Adyen dashboard, trigger order cancellation in NewStore OMS via MuleSoft and initiate a refund to the customer via Adyen to the original payment method. SFCC will receive the updated cancelled order status from NewStore OMS and reflect this to the customer. | Mule Integrator | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-051> |\n| PAY-053 | Cross-Border Checkout & Global-e | The system will identify whether an order is domestic or international based on the client's selected shipping country. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-053> |\n| PAY-054 | Cross-Border Checkout & Global-e | The system will redirect international customers to the Global-e checkout when they click Checkout from both the mini bag and the bag. | Accenture | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-054> |\n| PAY-055 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display the mini cart subtotal with a tax label indicating whether the amount is inclusive or exclusive of applicable tax, configured per storefront. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-055> |\n| PAY-056 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display the cart order summary with itemised tax line items: subtotal (incl/excl tax) and tax amount - values and labels configured per storefront. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-056> |\n| PAY-057 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display the checkout order summary with itemised tax line items: subtotal (incl/excl tax) and tax amount - values and labels configured per storefront. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-057> |\n| PAY-058 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display tax and duties as separate line items in the order breakdown - tax and duties must not be combined into a single line item. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-058> |\n| PAY-059 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display country-specific DDP/DDU messaging on the PDP page for applicable countries | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-059> |\n| PAY-060 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display country-specific DDP/DDU messaging on the mini-cart page for applicable countries | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-060> |\n| PAY-061 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display country-specific DDP/DDU messaging on the cart page for applicable countries | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-061> |\n| PAY-062 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display a Duties and Taxes hyperlink within the checkout disclaimer, navigating the client to further information on duties and tax obligations, for applicable countries | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-062> |\n| PAY-063 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will display the applicable tax label per storefront (e.g. GST for AU, VAT for UK and EU, Tax for US and HK) and pass this label to Narvar in the order data to support accurate display in the returns and tracking flow. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-063> |\n| PAY-064 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will pass the unit tax value divided by quantity to Narvar for line items with multiple quantities, to support accurate tax display in the returns flow. | Accenture | US (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-064> |\n| PAY-066 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will receive HS codes from AP21 (generated by Avalara, stored in AP21 custom fields per country). For international orders via Global-e, SFCC will pass HS codes to Global-e for duty and tax calculation. For cross-border orders on domestic storefronts (e.g. NZ customers on the AU storefront), SFCC will store and pass HS codes to Avalara for duty and tax calculation. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DPAY-066> |\n| PAY-067 | Tax & Duties Display | The system will use Avalara for tax calculation on the following: US domestic orders (variable state sales tax), New Zealand orders (GST/VAT and duties), and New Caledonia orders (GST/VAT and duties). For all other domestic storefronts, tax calculation will be handled via SFCC native tax tables | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <h