    "content": {
      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed.— source of truth. Req ID prefix: **RRC**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Req ID** | **Functional Area** | **Sub-Functional Area** | **Requirement** | **Owner** | **Storefront** | **Config/Custom** | **Status** | **Comments** | User Stories |\n| RRC-001 | Returns Eligibility | Returns Initiation | The system will allow products to be marked as not eligible for return at SKU level. A business user will be able to bulk-update the non-returnable flag at category level, with SKU-level settings taking precedence where set. | Accenture | ALL | Config | Confirmed | Additional Notes: Items ineligible for return: Gift cards (physical and virtual); Final sale items, which are clearly flagged. Items don't usually change from returnable to non-returnable during sales and seasonal campaigns. | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-001> |\n| RRC-002 | Returns Eligibility | Returns Initiation | The system will display a message for any products which are not eligible for return in the cart, mini-cart, and through checkout. The message must be configurable by a business user. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-002> |\n| RRC-003 | Returns Eligibility | Returns Initiation | The system will display a non-returnable / final sale indicator on the PDP for any product flagged as ineligible for return, so the customer is informed prior to purchase. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-003> |\n| RRC-004 | Returns Eligibility | Returns Initiation | The system will display a returns link on the order detail page in My Account, directing the customer to the appropriate returns portal. For domestic orders (AU, US, UK, HK), the system will link to the Narvar Returns Portal. For international orders, the system will link to the Global-e returns portal | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-003> |\n| RRC-005 | Returns Eligibility | Returns Initiation | The system will allow guest users to initiate a return, by asking them to enter their billing email and order number | Zimmerman | ALL |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-005> |\n| ~~RRC-006~~ | ~~Returns Eligibility~~ | ~~Returns Initiation~~ | ~~The system shall be able to show a different returns link for each of the EU countries~~ | ~~Accenture~~ | ~~ALL~~ | ~~Custom~~ | ~~Open~~ | Decscoped - all URLs are the same | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-006> |\n| RRC-007 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system will display return history on the Returns page in My Account by calling the MuleSoft /api/returns experience API (GET /api/returns?customer\\_id=), which consolidates return data from NewStore OMS. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-007> |\n| RRC-008 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system will display the status of the return on the Return History and Return detail page, as returned from NewStore via MuleSoft | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-008> |\n| RRC-009 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system shall display a separate Returns page in My Account, which will show all completed returns (no in-progress returns). | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-009> |\n| RRC-010 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system shall display a list of completed returns on the Returns page, including the total refund amount, the original order ID, and the return completed date. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-010> |\n| RRC-011 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system shall have a Return Detail page for each return in My Account, displaying relevant return fields. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-011> |\n| RRC-012 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system shall display a Cancelled status label on the Order History page for fully cancelled orders, distinct from Returned status. | Zimmerman | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-012> |\n| RRC-013 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system shall surface order status on the Order History page by calling the MuleSoft Experience API (GET /api/orders?customer\\_id=); status shall be retrieved on page load. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-013> |\n| RRC-014 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system shall display the return status received from NewStore via MuleSoft on the Returns page for each return; status shall be retrieved on page load. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-014> |\n| RRC-015 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system will not display refund status directly to the customer. | Zimmerman | ALL |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-015> |\n| RRC-016 | Cancellation Refund & Confirmation | Order Cancellations | The system will surface cancellation status on the order detail page in My Account once updated by the OMS via MuleSoft. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-016> |\n| RRC-017 | BOPIS & Specialist Cancellations | Order Cancellations | The system will display BOPIS cancellation status in My Account once the order has been cancelled by the OMS. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-017> |\n| RRC-018 | Cancellation Refund & Confirmation | Order Cancellations | The system will be able to display partially cancelled orders in My Account Order History and My Account Order Detail, where an order may be partially cancelled (full order, individual line item, or partial line item), as returned from NewStore via MuleSoft. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-018> |\n| ~~RRC-019~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will allow an authorised CS agent to open a storefront session as a registered customer to place an order on their behalf (Order on Behalf Of - OOBO).~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-020~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will allow an authorised CS agent to search for the customer by email in Business Manager and open an OOBO session; this will redirect to the storefront in agent mode.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-021~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will display a banner on top of the storefront to confirm the OOBO context.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Ready for Sign Off~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-022~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will allow an authorised CS agent within the OOBO session to: browse the full product catalogue; add items to cart; apply or remove coupon codes; select a shipping address from saved addresses; select a shipping method.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-023~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will allow an authorised CS agent to apply manual price adjustments at line-item and order level, and override the shipping charge - subject to their assigned Business Manager role permissions.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Ready for Sign Off~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-024~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will allow an authorised CS agent to make payment via stored card within an OOBO session: if the customer has a tokenised payment method saved in SFCC (via Adyen), the agent may select it at checkout - no raw card data is entered.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-025~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will allow an authorised CS agent to initiate an Adyen pay-by-link within an OOBO session when no stored card is available; the customer completes payment independently via the link - no raw card data is entered or handled by the agent.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-026~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Orders placed via OOBO will be attributed to the customer and appear in the customer's My Account order history under their account.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-027~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~OOBO orders will follow the standard SFCC order pipeline - export to MuleSoft and routing to NewStore OMS applies as per all other orders.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-028~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Orders placed via OOBO will carry an agent identifier attribute, capturing the CS agent who placed the order. This attribute will be passed to MuleSoft and NewStore OMS to support reporting and commission attribution.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| ~~RRC-029~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~Manual Orders – OOBO~~ | ~~The system will restrict access to OOBO order placement to authorised CS agent roles configured in SFCC Business Manager.~~ | ~~Dependent SF Functionality~~ | ~~ALL~~ |  | ~~Confirmed~~ | Descoped |  |\n| RRC-030 | Returns Display in My Account | Returns Initiation | The system must be able to, on the Return Detail page, accommodate for different taxes and duties display per country. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Narvar/Global-e/or NewStore? @Manikandan Ramachandran (Deactivated) @Tim Lavelle to check API to see if we can provide this | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-030> |\n| RRC-031 | Returns Eligibility | Returns Initiation | The system must display a returns policy link within the terms acceptance copy at checkout; clicking the link must open the /returns page in a new browser tab. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DRRC-031> |",
