{"result":"{
  "id": "340000846",
  "title": "9. Payment Configuration",
  "type": "page",
  "created": "",
  "updated": "",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/340000846",
  "space": {
    "key": "SFCC",
    "name": "Adobe SFCC"
  },
  "version": 2,
  "attachments": [],
  "content": {
    "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nPayment configuration in BM determines which payment methods appear at checkout and in what order. Production payment credentials must never be sandbox/test keys. Given Zimmermann's dual-gateway model (Adyen for domestic, Global-e for international) and BNPL (Afterpay/Clearpay) this requires careful per-site verification.\n\n**📎 Salesforce Docs:** [Payment Methods in Business Manager](https://documentation.b2c.commercecloud.salesforce.com/DOC2/topic/com.demandware.dochelp/Payments/PaymentMethods.html)  \n**📎 Adyen Docs:** [Adyen SFCC Cartridge Configuration](https://docs.adyen.com/plugins/salesforce-commerce-cloud/)  \n**📎 Global-e Docs:** [Global-e Merchant Portal](https://www.global-e.com/merchants/)\n\n**⚠️ Risk note:** Sandbox/test payment credentials reaching production is a P1 go-live blocker. Verify Adyen and PayPal API keys are production credentials on every site. This is the single most common payment-related launch failure.\n\n---\n\nChecklist\n---------\n\n### Global Payment Setup (BM: Merchant Tools → Ordering → Payment Methods)\n\nincompleteAll demo/placeholder payment methods **removed**\nincompletePayment method display order confirmed correct per site\nincompleteAll payment methods tested end-to-end in UAT with real (non-sandbox) card numbers\n\n### Adyen — Domestic Markets\n\nincompleteAdyen cartridge installed and configured in BM\nincomplete**Production** Adyen API key configured — not sandbox key\nincompleteAdyen merchant account confirmed as production account\nincompleteAdyen webhook endpoint configured and receiving events (order status, refunds)\nincomplete3DS2 configured and tested with Adyen\nincompleteCredit card (Visa, Mastercard, Amex) tested in UAT\nincompleteApple Pay tested (requires domain verification with Apple)\nincompleteGoogle Pay tested\nincompleteAdyen Fraud Management rules configured for production thresholds\n\n### PayPal\n\nincompletePayPal **production** API credentials configured — not sandbox\nincompletePayPal payment method enabled per relevant sites\nincompletePayPal flow tested end-to-end\n\n### Afterpay (AU) / Clearpay (UK)\n\nincompleteAfterpay configured for AU site with **production** credentials\nincompleteClearpay configured for UK site with **production** credentials\nincompleteBNPL instalment messaging visible on PDP and cart\nincompleteOrder limits for BNPL verified (min/max order value)\n\n### Givex — Gift Cards\n\nincompleteGivex integration configured in BM with production credentials\nincompleteGift card balance check working at checkout\nincompleteGift card partial payment (split with another payment method) tested\n\n### Global-e — International Checkout (US Intl, EU Intl, ME, HK)\n\nincompleteSFCC payment method for Global-e redirect configured\nincompleteShoppers on Global-e storefronts are correctly redirected to Global-e checkout\nincompleteGlobal-e is handling duties, taxes, and localised payment methods for international sites\nincompleteGlobal-e production merchant account confirmed — not test/sandbox\n\n### Avalara — Tax (Domestic)\n\nincompleteAvalara production credentials configured in BM\nincompleteTax calculation tested on AU, UK, US Domestic orders\nincompleteTax calculation not firing on Global-e storefronts (Global-e handles tax for international)\n\n\n---\n\nNotes / Findings\n----------------\n\n*Record gaps, decisions, and owner for remediation here.*\n\n| Finding | Severity | Owner | Resolved |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  |  |  |",
    "format": "markdown"
  },
  "emoji": "1f4b3"
}"}

